Enter following into Powershell:

1) docker ps                      # confirm mongo-dbserver shows "Up"

2) Ping mongo-dbserver            # confirm it resolves to 127.0.0.1

3) Select-String -Path C:\Windows\System32\drivers\etc\hosts -Pattern "mongo-dbserver"

If fails, do the following:

1) If DOCKER PS doesn't show container: docker start mongo-dbserver

2) If PING MONGO-DBSERVER fails: hosts file entry got wiped, re-add it in notepad (as administrator):
    2.1) Run Notepad as administrator. File > Open
    2.2) Navigate: C:\WIndows\System32\drivers\etc
    2.3) Select 'hosts' file. Open.
    2.4) Add line to end of file: 127.0.0.1 mongo-dbserver
    2.5) Ctrl+S to save.
    2.6) Verify in powershell with: ping mongo-dbserver
    2.7) Test whether running App.java / App.jar work
